{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the Eulerian number A(n, m).\n\n    - Valid inputs: integers n >= 0, integer m.\n    - By convention: if m < 0 or m >= n (except the special case n == 0 and m == 0),\n      the function returns 0.\n    - Raises ValueError for invalid n (non-integer or negative).\n    \"\"\"\n    def _ensure_int(value, name: str) -> int:\n        if isinstance(value, bool):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be an integer (bool is not accepted)\")\n        if isinstance(value, int):\n            return value\n        if isinstance(value, float) and value.is_integer():\n            return int(value)\n        raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be an integer\")\n\n    n = _ensure_int(n, \"n\")\n    m = _ensure_int(m, \"m\")\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be non-negative\")\n\n    # Special base case\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Business rule: out-of-range m returns 0\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Iterative DP using only previous row; we only compute columns up to m.\n    prev = [1]  # A(0,0) = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # We only need values for j = 0..min(i, m)\n        max_j = min(i, m)\n        curr = [0] * (max_j + 1)\n        for j in range(0, max_j + 1):\n            term1 = (i - j) * prev[j - 1] if j - 1 >= 0 and (j - 1) < len(prev) else 0\n            term2 = (j + 1) * prev[j] if j < len(prev) else 0\n            curr[j] = term1 + term2\n        prev = curr\n\n    return prev[m]"}
