{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(s: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of times a binary string, when rotated, results in an odd number.\n    An odd number in binary has its least significant bit (rightmost digit) as '1'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str) or not s:\n        raise ValueError(\"s must be a non-empty binary string\")\n    if any(ch not in \"01\" for ch in s):\n        raise ValueError(\"s must contain only '0' or '1'\")\n    if not isinstance(rotations, int) or rotations < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"rotations must be a non-negative integer\")\n\n    n = len(s)\n    if rotations == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    ones_in_full_cycle = s.count(\"1\")\n    full_cycles_count = rotations // n\n    remainder_rotations = rotations % n\n\n    total_odd_count = full_cycles_count * ones_in_full_cycle\n\n    # For remainder rotations, count last-bit positions in order: n-1, 0, 1, ...\n    for i in range(remainder_rotations):\n        idx = (n - 1 + i) % n\n        if s[idx] == \"1\":\n            total_odd_count += 1\n\n    return total_odd_count"}
