{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum difference between the number of 0s and 1s in any substring\n    of the given binary string using Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str) or len(s) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-empty binary string containing only '0' and '1'.\")\n\n    # Validate characters are only '0' or '1'\n    for ch in s:\n        if ch not in {\"0\", \"1\"}:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must contain only '0' and '1' characters.\")\n\n    # Convert binary string to weights: '0' -> +1, '1' -> -1\n    weights = [1 if char == '0' else -1 for char in s]\n\n    # Kadane's algorithm to find maximum subarray sum\n    max_ending_here = max_so_far = weights[0]\n    for w in weights[1:]:\n        max_ending_here = max(w, max_ending_here + w)\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
