{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "class SumRangeError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for sum range operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(message)\nclass IndexRangeError(SumRangeError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when resolved indices are out of valid list bounds.\"\"\"\n    pass\nclass ArgumentError(SumRangeError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when start index is greater than end index after resolution.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef _resolve_indices(lst: list, start: int, end: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Resolves negative indices to positive and validates the index range.\"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    resolved_start = start if start >= 0 else n + start\n    resolved_end = end if end >= 0 else n + end\n\n    # Validate individual resolved indices against list bounds\n    if not (0 <= resolved_start < n) or not (0 <= resolved_end < n):\n        raise IndexRangeError(\"Resolved indices out of range.\")\n\n    # Validate the order of resolved indices\n    if resolved_start > resolved_end:\n        raise ArgumentError(\"start index must be <= end index after resolution.\")\n\n    return resolved_start, resolved_end\ndef sum_range_list(lst: list, start: int, end: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of elements in a list over a contiguous index range (inclusive).\n    Validates inputs and handles negative indices according to Python's semantics.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_list_contents(lst)\n    resolved_start, resolved_end = _resolve_indices(lst, start, end)\n\n    # Python slices are exclusive for the end index, so add 1 to include the resolved_end element.\n    sublist = lst[resolved_start : resolved_end + 1]\n    total = sum(sublist)\n    return float(total)"}
