{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of sequences of length n, where each element is a positive integer.\n    Each element must be greater than or equal to twice the previous element and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(m, int) or not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"m and n must be integers\")\n    if m < 1 or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"m and n must be positive integers (>= 1)\")\n\n    # dp[k][x] stores the number of valid sequences of length k that start with x.\n    # We only need the previous layer's counts to compute the current layer's counts.\n\n    # Base case: For sequences of length 1, any integer x from 1 to m is valid.\n    prev = [0] * (m + 1)\n    for x in range(1, m + 1):\n        prev[x] = 1\n\n    # Iterate for sequence lengths (layers) from 2 up to n.\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        curr = [0] * (m + 1)\n\n        # Calculate prefix sums of the 'prev' array to efficiently compute suffix sums.\n        prefix = [0] * (m + 1)\n        running_sum = 0\n        for i in range(1, m + 1):\n            running_sum += prev[i]\n            prefix[i] = running_sum\n\n        total_sum_prev = prefix[m]\n\n        # For each possible starting value 'x' in the current layer.\n        for x in range(1, m + 1):\n            min_next_val = 2 * x\n            if min_next_val > m:\n                curr[x] = 0\n            else:\n                curr[x] = total_sum_prev - prefix[min_next_val - 1]\n\n        prev = curr\n\n    return sum(prev[1:])"}
