{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "def next_Perfect_Square(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the smallest perfect square strictly greater than n.\n\n    - If n is a float it will be converted to int via truncation (int(n)).\n    - Raises ValueError for None or non-finite floats (NaN/Inf) or values not convertible to int.\n    \"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    if n is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a number\")\n\n    # Reject non-finite floats\n    if isinstance(n, float):\n        if math.isnan(n) or math.isinf(n):\n            raise ValueError(\"n must be finite\")\n\n    try:\n        ni = int(n)\n    except Exception:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer or convertible to int\")\n\n    # For negative integers, 0 is a perfect square and is strictly greater than any negative n\n    if ni < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    r = math.isqrt(ni)\n    # If ni is a perfect square (r*r == ni) or r*r < ni, we need the next integer r+1\n    if r * r <= ni:\n        k = r + 1\n    else:\n        k = r\n\n    return k * k"}
