{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sort the given array using Shell Sort (Knuth gap sequence).\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, (list, tuple)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list or tuple of integers\")\n    a = list(arr)\n    n = len(a)\n\n    # Generate Knuth's gap sequence: 1, 4, 13, 40, ...\n    gaps = []\n    h = 1\n    while h < n:\n        gaps.append(h)\n        h = 3 * h + 1\n\n    # Perform gapped insertion sort for each gap (largest to smallest)\n    for gap in reversed(gaps):\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = a[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and a[j - gap] > temp:\n                a[j] = a[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            a[j] = temp\n\n    return a"}
