{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of elements from two tuples of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        a (tuple): Outer tuple of inner tuples with numeric elements.\n        b (tuple): Outer tuple of inner tuples with numeric elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        tuple: A tuple of tuples where each inner tuple contains products of corresponding elements.\n\n    Note:\n        This function assumes the inputs are well-formed: same outer length, each pair of inner tuples\n        at the same index have the same length, and all elements are numeric. It does not perform validation.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(a)):\n        inner_result = []\n        for j in range(len(a[i])):\n            inner_result.append(a[i][j] * b[i][j])\n        result.append(tuple(inner_result))\n    return tuple(result)"}
