{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(sublists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the first sublist (element of the outer sequence) that has the minimum length.\n\n    Args:\n        sublists: a non-empty sequence (typically list or tuple) of sequences (e.g. lists or tuples).\n\n    Returns:\n        The sublist from the input that has the smallest length. If multiple sublists tie,\n        the first occurrence is returned.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: if the outer object or any element is not a sequence (list/tuple).\n        ValueError: if the outer sequence is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(sublists, (list, tuple)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list or tuple of sequences\")\n    if len(sublists) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-empty sequence of sequences\")\n\n    try:\n        min_len = len(sublists[0])\n    except TypeError:\n        raise TypeError(\"Each element must be a sequence (have a length)\")\n\n    min_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, len(sublists)):\n        s = sublists[i]\n        try:\n            l = len(s)\n        except TypeError:\n            raise TypeError(\"Each element must be a sequence (have a length)\")\n        if l < min_len:\n            min_len = l\n            min_idx = i\n\n    return sublists[min_idx]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/455", "solution": "def check_monthnumb_number(month: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return True if the given month number (1-12) has 31 days, otherwise False.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: if `month` is not an integer in the range 1..12.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Reject booleans (bool is a subclass of int) and ensure integer type\n    if isinstance(month, bool) or not isinstance(month, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"month must be an integer between 1 and 12\")\n\n    if not 1 <= month <= 12:\n        raise ValueError(\"month must be an integer between 1 and 12\")\n\n    return month in {1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12}"}
