{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Optional\ndef triangle_area(radius: float) -> Optional[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the area of the largest triangle that can be inscribed in a semicircle with a given radius.\n    Returns float area or None if radius is invalid (e.g., negative, non-numeric, or non-finite).\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        r_float = float(radius)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError):\n        return None\n\n    if math.isinf(r_float) or math.isnan(r_float) or r_float < 0:\n        return None\n\n    # The largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle has its base as the diameter (2*R)\n    # and its height as the radius (R). Area = 0.5 * base * height = 0.5 * (2*R) * R = R^2.\n    return r_float * r_float"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/631", "solution": "def replace_spaces(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces whitespaces with an underscore or vice versa based on string content.\n    Whitespace runs are collapsed to a single underscore; each underscore becomes a single space.\n    \"\"\"\n    import re\n\n    if '_' in input_string and not re.search(r'\\s', input_string):\n        # If underscores are present and no other whitespace, replace underscores with spaces\n        return input_string.replace('_', ' ')\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, replace any sequence of whitespace characters with a single underscore\n        return re.sub(r'\\s+', '_', input_string)"}
