{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr, value) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index or -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1  # Initialize result to -1 (not found)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == value:\n            result = mid  # Found a match, store its index\n            low = mid + 1 # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < value:\n            low = mid + 1 # Value is in the right half\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1 # Value is in the left half\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/792", "solution": "def count_list(data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the number of top-level Python list instances in the given input.\n\n    Examples:\n        assert count_list([[1, 3], [5, 7], [9, 11], [13, 15, 17]]) == 4\n    \"\"\"\n    if data is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"input cannot be None\")\n\n    # Normalize common iterables to a list, but treat strings/bytes as invalid\n    if isinstance(data, (list, tuple)):\n        items = list(data)\n    elif hasattr(data, \"__iter__\") and not isinstance(data, (str, bytes)):\n        items = list(data)\n    else:\n        raise TypeError(\"input must be an iterable (list/tuple) of items; strings are not allowed\")\n\n    return sum(1 for elem in items if isinstance(elem, list))"}
